# Local workspace state — never commit. If someone runs qj with the repo as its
# workspace (or QJ_WORKSPACE points inside it), these appear here:
#   browser_profile/  Playwright/Chromium profile: live SSO cookies, tokens, and
#                     saved logins after `qj browser login`, plus machine-specific
#                     caches. Nothing in a browser profile belongs in a shared repo
#                     — the session files are credentials, the rest is disposable
#                     cache. Each user runs `qj browser login` on their own machine.
#   .session          the CLI's bearer token (a live credential)
#   /config.yaml      a real workspace config may hold literal secrets
#                     (config.example.yaml is the tracked template)
browser_profile/
.session
/config.yaml
briefs/
exports/
repos/
evals/
